{"title":"2026 AMC 8 Regional Problems/Problem 15","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem_15\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 15</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2_(Brute_Force)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2 (Brute Force)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_15\">Problem 15</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_AMC_8_Regional_Problems/Problem_15&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 15\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Jami rolls two standard six-sided dice. What is the probability that the two digits rolled can be arranged to form a two-digit number divisible by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/1/e/61ec0637bcdce417958332de92b54c25524d88ac.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ \\frac{1}{4}\\qquad\\textbf{(B)}\\ \\frac{1}{3}\\qquad\\textbf{(C)}\\ \\frac{13}{36}\\qquad\\textbf{(D)}\\ \\frac{5}{12}\\qquad\\textbf{(E)}\\ \\frac{17}{36}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"398\" height=\"38\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_AMC_8_Regional_Problems/Problem_15&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>When rolling two standard six-sided dice, there are a total of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/9/7/897dd68f9e342665851f9e9b91b87a28d42fc7e2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6 \\times 6 = 36$\" width=\"82\" height=\"12\" /> equally likely outcomes. We want to find how many pairs of faces can be rearranged into a two-digit number that is a multiple of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. The possible two-digit multiples of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> that can be formed using only the digits <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> through <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/1/601a7806cbfad68196c43a4665871f8c3186802e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/f/edf074831eb5bc9e61d6d6e09f525a86e3068f6a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$12$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/5/9a5b4928c8fe50ce3c2428da3bee3505e891b788.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$16$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/9/e290f2cba0ba0e11c0b91630da15a408da2fcf1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$24$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/f/4/4f4b8590f8aa9f9894b3891dd5dede0e354fa04e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$32$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/e/5/ce5d3cbb9ab0a992ed503c2d4499e4f4af2f9d65.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$36$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/b/4/5b45828f292e161290be6ee62bc4c9df081ee1e1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$44$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/e/1/5e1d1611143f5792dc0f61f3b130af88cb790c04.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$52$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/3/9/6392be3c4d257afbc7ed9283bdb8ba630f4ef7e1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$56$\" width=\"17\" height=\"12\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/5/e/05e228ac5bee7b9ffb60cacf50f3f2c7c31f8038.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$64$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"18\" height=\"13\" />. Now we track which unique dice outcomes can produce these numbers. The outcomes where the two dice show different digits are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/1/3/71350a031d3d4f8a3fdd44b2d1514a1557eff1ae.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\{1,2\\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"43\" height=\"18\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/1/b/e1b6a1aa9230116f679bc3ef4a620376c70231df.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\{1,6\\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"43\" height=\"18\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/9/9/399e827e5e2ed8536404998d419e8d38851fc2e9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\{2,4\\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"43\" height=\"18\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/e/c/aecde0f67320bdda3e42e9c518e030378f7d9251.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\{2,3\\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"46\" height=\"20\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/3/f/43f06a91794b3622faa21966323532b2785e0f35.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\{3,6\\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"46\" height=\"20\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/4/b/f4b63054f0ee7f34113c73a14c252fb1e118e102.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\{2,5\\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"46\" height=\"20\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/2/f/f2f37550cd07c47152dc40bec049469bf6663da3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\{5,6\\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"46\" height=\"20\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/2/f/d2f3d303b165b6a88f0cb69b27fe941115a811c9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\{4,6\\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"46\" height=\"20\" />. Each of these <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/5/8455f3b5cb3b4880b8c9d782a5c1f0334db819eb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> unique pairs can be rolled in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> different orders (for example, rolling a <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, or a <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />), giving <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/4/6/d462bb87c4d426f8ad25ea45066078a3fb0e6e9b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$8 \\times 2 = 16$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"82\" height=\"13\" /> outcomes. The only multiple with identical digits is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/b/4/5b45828f292e161290be6ee62bc4c9df081ee1e1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$44$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />, which comes from the single unique outcome <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/e/7/9e74a8a996f28bdc445eb3beaf3c3f14594eac27.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(4,4)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"38\" height=\"18\" />. Adding these together, there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/5/6/8562e5012440817ee7b4fbcbe37d1b0811806871.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$16 + 1 = 17$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"94\" height=\"15\" /> successful outcomes out of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/e/5/ce5d3cbb9ab0a992ed503c2d4499e4f4af2f9d65.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$36$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> total possibilities.\n</p><p>The correct answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/e/7/5e7d35fcb32eb747c6832b54f4f7b132a3d680bc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(E)}\\ \\frac{17}{36}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -19px\" width=\"68\" height=\"49\" />.\n</p><p>~Icosahedron0288\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_2_.28Brute_Force.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2_(Brute_Force)\">Solution 2 (Brute Force)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_AMC_8_Regional_Problems/Problem_15&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2 (Brute Force)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Another way to find the total amount of successful outcomes is literally brute forcing it\n</p><p>Doubles have a <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/f/bcf4ee57cbce0ef6a5c3bbf4ce51e5ea29450aa8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1/36$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"35\" height=\"18\" /> chance, while singles have a <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/4/3/1430db4a63117bb7bc318d8d56d68c25879bdfa4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1/18$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"38\" height=\"20\" />.\n</p><p>Successful: 12, 16, 32, 24, 52, 36, 44, 64, 56\n</p><p>Not successful: 11, 13, 14, 15, 22, 26, 33, 34, 35, 45, 55, 66\n</p><p>There are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/4/2/942406ff49f6d27f36ffe86f13b57601b402821c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2 \\times 8 = 16$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"85\" height=\"15\" /> for the doubles, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> for the singles. \n</p><p>Therefore, there is a total of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/5/6/8562e5012440817ee7b4fbcbe37d1b0811806871.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$16 + 1 = 17$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"94\" height=\"15\" /> possibilities, and 36 total possibilities. \n</p><p>The correct answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/e/7/5e7d35fcb32eb747c6832b54f4f7b132a3d680bc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(E)}\\ \\frac{17}{36}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -19px\" width=\"68\" height=\"49\" />.\n</p><p>~xue1\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_AMC_8_Regional_Problems/Problem_15&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_AMC_8_Regional_Problems\" title=\"2026 AMC 8 Regional Problems\">2026 AMC 8 Regional Problems</a></li></ul>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017164204\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.017 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.028 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 221/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 0/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 2/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 7480/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    0.000      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:37398:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017164204 and revision id 292007. Rendering was triggered because: page-view\n -->\n</div>"}